# Antigravity Workspace Rules: Buddhilive Academy

## 1. Grounding Rule
- Whenever creating, editing, or outlining lessons, inspect `/docs` first.
- Every code snippet, algorithm, and concept must cite and derive from the reference documents in `/docs`.

## 2. Content Generation Contract
- Every lesson must be an `.mdx` file located in `/src/content/lessons/`.
- Frontmatter must strictly validate against our Zod schema: `title`, `topic`, `difficulty`, `xp`, `prerequisites`.
- Each lesson must contain at least 350+ words of clear conceptual explanation with KaTeX formulas before or alongside interactive widgets (ensuring high-quality AdSense indexing).
- Use `<PythonRunner client:visible />` for interactive code execution. Code execution must never block the main thread.

## 3. Code Integrity & Architecture
- Maintain clean separation between static layout and hydrated islands.
- Zero-Backend / 100% Client-Side Execution: All Python runs client-side via Pyodide v0.26+ in a Web Worker (`/src/workers/pyodide.worker.ts`) with a hard 5-second timeout.
- Never introduce Node/server-side dependencies for code execution.
- Offline-first state persistence in `localStorage`, syncing to Supabase (PostgreSQL + RLS) when authenticated.

## 4. Theme & Styling
- Project must support light and dark mode with `#A7452A` as primary color (with dark mode tint `#E07A5F`).
- All interactive elements and colors must meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast standards.
- Reserve fixed container heights for Google AdSense slots to eliminate Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS).
